"answer": "The sources do not list a rate for a 20-user septic tank that is 0.5 m longer than standard. The standard 20-user item is S-3.28.2 (230 x 110 x 150 cm), a complete item rate of Rs. 35868.00 per Each [S1]. This is the rate for the standard size only. The only length-adjustment note, '-12.5% Breadth & Depth -18 % each' per 0.5 M change in length, is printed under S-3.28.3, the 50-user tank (400 x 140 x 150 cm) [S2]. In the S-3.28 listing, S-3.28.2 carries no such note [S3]. So the sources do not confirm that the 12.5% adjustment applies to the 20-user tank. If the note were applied to S-3.28.2 by analogy, which the sources do not state, the arithmetic would be 12.5% × 35868 = 4483.50, giving 35868 + 4483.50 = Rs. 40351.50. This figure is only an illustration, not a listed rate. Confirm with the competent authority which rate to use.",
"missing": "No rate or rule in the sources for increasing the length of the 20-user septic tank (S-3.28.2). The proportional-adjustment note appears only under the 50-user item S-3.28.3, and the sources do not say whether it extends to S-3.28.2."}

