  "answer": "The Rajasthan PWD tender notice excerpts provided do not say what happens when a bidder quotes nil rates against every item. [S2][S6][S8] Under the CPWD General Conditions of Contract, which is a different central-government contract, the tender is treated as invalid if a tenderer quotes nil rates against each item in an item rate tender. [S1] That tender will not be considered as lowest tenderer. [S1] The earnest money deposited is forfeited. [S1] This CPWD rule is separate from the case where only some items are left blank: if no rate is quoted for an item and the figures, words and amount are all blank, the cost is presumed included in other items and the rate is taken as zero. [S1]",
