"answer": "The question's premise does not match the sources. The cap on total compensation for delay in completion under Clause 2 is 10% of the accepted Tendered Value of the work (or of the sectional part, as in Schedule 'F'), not 5% [S3]. Clause 2 also sets a maximum rate of 1% per month of delay, computed on a per-day basis [S3]. The 5% figure comes from Clause 19J. If a completed building is illegally occupied, the Engineer-in-Charge may refuse to accept it [S2]. Any resulting delay in acceptance is treated as delay in completion, and the Superintending Engineer may impose a levy of up to 5% of the tendered value, with a final decision on justification and amount [S1]. The sources do not give any reason or rationale for why either percentage was chosen.",
"missing": "The sources do not explain why the 10% cap (Clause 2) or the 5% levy limit (Clause 19J) were set at those levels. They also do not say that total compensation is capped at 5%."}

